# Office layer — read the domain file before editing

**[`docs/agents/domains/office.md`](../../docs/agents/domains/office.md)**

Read its **Short form** first, then the **Full findings** entry for whatever you are changing.
This content used to sit in the root `CLAUDE.md` (48 KB) and `AGENTS.md` (27 KB) at once, loaded by
every session in this repo. Same content, one copy, four agents.

The two rules everything else follows from:

- **Ambient vs reactive** (`docs/office-parody.md` § 11). A timer interrupted you → stay
  canned-heavy. You started it or answered it → lean LLM, because a canned reply to a sentence you
  typed is the clearest possible tell that nobody is home. The appetite table is one file:
  `officeCadence.js`. Tune there, not at the use site.
- **Record, never trigger** (ADR-0010 consequence #4). The office log, working memory and the
  errand all *record*. The moment one of them schedules or fires something, it is
  auto-fix-on-idle in a new hat.

Two that will cost you an afternoon:

- **Any floor test that _mounts_ inherits the wall clock and `Math.random`.** Pin both. A suite
  that passes standalone and fails in file order — or passes for 16 hours a day — is this.
- **Exactly one surface may draw a person.** `settledIds` is the hand-off; miss it and a scene
  ends with people blinking back into chairs while their own figures are still crossing the room.

**Add findings to the domain file, once.** Do not copy them back into the root files; that
mirroring rule is retired for domain content (`docs/routines/README.md` rule 8).
